rem and either makes real progress or bails early with a diagnosis. NO fullscreen workaround.
call "%~dp0run-mcp.cmd" "Using ONLY the windows-computer-use MCP tools (do not use Bash): open a web browser to https://www.coolmathgames.com/0-bloxorz and play Bloxorz - roll the 1x2 block with the ARROW KEYS into the square hole. Click through ads/menus/tutorial into Stage 1. KEY TECHNIQUE for browser games: to give the game canvas keyboard focus, put a left_click ON THE GAME CANVAS in the SAME act batch immediately before the arrow key, and do NOT take a screenshot between the click and the key. Do NOT use the game's fullscreen mode. Verify each move actually happened by checking the on-screen Moves counter (it should increment). Use the record tool to capture a short video clip (~6-8s) while making moves so there is an mp4 to review. Make at least 5-6 real moves toward the hole. Report whether keyboard input worked (did Moves increment?), what you saw on the board, and the exact mp4 path."
